(425352, 37524, 10643, '<td valign="top">The background is grainy because it''s the back of a presswood serving tray. That''s just what it looks like. For those who took issue with the title, the red area (50 points) is the "cork," and the term "bull''s-eye" refers both to the cork (or "double bull") and the green area (25 points), the "single bull." So I didn''t make a mistake with the titling or the aim. It landed in the green, a bull''s-eye.</td>', 'The background is grainy because it''s the back of a presswood serving tray. That''s just what it looks like. For those who took issue with the title, the red area (50 points) is the "cork," and the term "bull''s-eye" refers both to the cork (or "double bull") and the green area (25 points), the "single bull." So I didn''t make a mistake with the titling or the aim. It landed in the green, a bull''s-eye.', '2003-09-22 01:08:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(425353, 37802, 7711, '<td valign="top">i knew this was you, arnit! :) Beautiful colour and perfect action! congratulations!</td>', 'i knew this was you, arnit! :) Beautiful colour and perfect action! congratulations!', '2003-09-22 01:08:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(425360, 37842, 10686, '<td valign="top">Wow, 6th place! Not bad for my 4th challenge. That sets a new high for me. Thanks everyone who voted, and especially everyone who left comments. Yes, the bike was on a wind trainer and those are my hairy legs. I used the remote to shoot while riding. My initial impulse was to make a bracket that mounted to the bike and held my camera, but I didn''t get time to shoot anything until about 9pm the night of the submission deadline. Barely made it. Minimal time to run it through PS. The difference in color balance between the flash and the tungsten light did kind of bother me and I''d probably take 2 shots and combine them in PS using layers, but that wouldn''t have been legal for the challenge.</td>', 'Wow, 6th place! Not bad for my 4th challenge. That sets a new high for me. Thanks everyone who voted, and especially everyone who left comments. Yes, the bike was on a wind trainer and those are my hairy legs. I used the remote to shoot while riding. My initial impulse was to make a bracket that mounted to the bike and held my camera, but I didn''t get time to shoot anything until about 9pm the night of the submission deadline. Barely made it. Minimal time to run it through PS. The difference in color balance between the flash and the tungsten light did kind of bother me and I''d probably take 2 shots and combine them in PS using layers, but that wouldn''t have been legal for the challenge.', '2003-09-22 01:11:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(425370, 37807, 10263, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon. Excellent shot</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon. Excellent shot', '2003-09-22 01:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
